.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt STDBIT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm stdc_leading_zeros ,
.Nm stdc_leading_ones ,
.Nm stdc_trailing_zeros ,
.Nm stdc_trailing_ones ,
.Nm stdc_first_leading_zero ,
.Nm stdc_first_leading_one ,
.Nm stdc_first_trailing_zero ,
.Nm stdc_first_trailing_one ,
.Nm stdc_count_zeros ,
.Nm stdc_count_ones ,
.Nm stdc_has_single_bit ,
.Nm stdc_bit_width ,
.Nm stdc_bit_floor ,
.Nm stdc_bit_ceil
.Nd bit and byte utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdbit.h
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_leading_zeros "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_leading_ones "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_trailing_zeros "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_trailing_ones "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_first_leading_zero "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_first_leading_one "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_first_trailing_zero "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_first_trailing_one "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_count_zeros "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_count_ones "unsigned int value"
.Ft bool
.Fn stdc_has_single_bit "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_bit_width "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_bit_floor "unsigned int value"
.Ft unsigned int
.Fn stdc_bit_ceil "unsigned int value"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.In stdbit.h
header provides the ISO C23 bit and byte utilities.
The functions above are type-generic macros that accept any unsigned
integer type; for each there are also typed functions with the suffixes
.Sy _uc ,
.Sy _us ,
.Sy _ui ,
.Sy _ul
and
.Sy _ull
for
.Vt unsigned char ,
.Vt unsigned short ,
.Vt unsigned int ,
.Vt unsigned long
and
.Vt unsigned long long .
.Pp
.Fn stdc_leading_zeros
and
.Fn stdc_trailing_zeros
count the number of consecutive zero bits starting from the most or least
significant bit; the corresponding
.Fn _ones
macros count one bits.
.Fn stdc_first_leading_zero ,
.Fn stdc_first_leading_one ,
.Fn stdc_first_trailing_zero
and
.Fn stdc_first_trailing_one
return the one-based position of the first matching bit, or zero if no
such bit exists.
.Fn stdc_count_zeros
and
.Fn stdc_count_ones
count all zero or one bits.
.Pp
.Fn stdc_bit_width
returns the number of bits needed to represent the value, ignoring
leading zeros;
.Fn stdc_bit_floor
returns the largest power of two not greater than the value, and
.Fn stdc_bit_ceil
the smallest power of two not less than the value.
Both return a value of the same type as their argument.
.Fn stdc_has_single_bit
reports whether the value is a power of two.
.Pp
The macros
.Dv __STDC_ENDIAN_LITTLE__ ,
.Dv __STDC_ENDIAN_BIG__
and
.Dv __STDC_ENDIAN_NATIVE__
are distinct integer constants;
.Dv __STDC_ENDIAN_NATIVE__
equals one of the other two according to the byte order of the machine.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The counting, searching and width functions return a value of type
.Vt unsigned int .
The first-bit searches return zero when no matching bit is present.
.Fn stdc_bit_floor
and
.Fn stdc_bit_ceil
return the type of their argument.
.Sh NOTES
The typed functions are libc entry points with external linkage and a
stable address.
The type-generic interface accepts the standard unsigned integer types and,
where the compiler provides a 128-bit integer type, that type as well; in
C++ it is provided with overloaded functions.
.Pp
The C29
.Fn stdc_rotate_left
and
.Fn stdc_rotate_right
additions are not part of ISO C23 and are not provided.
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.In stdbit.h
header conforms to ISO/IEC 9899:2024 (C23).
.Sh HISTORY
The
.In stdbit.h
header appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
